{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-04b32baa", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2604.21670 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2604.21670 reports 12 systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Diboson cross-section theoretical uncertainty\n- Electron and muon reconstruction, identification, trigger efficiency and energy scale/resolution uncertainties\n- Flavour tagging uncertainty\n- Higgs boson branching ratio uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Pile-up modelling uncertainty\n- Single top theoretical modelling uncertainty\n- Tau-lepton reconstruction/identification uncertainty\n- WW modelling uncertainty\n- Z+jets modelling uncertainty\n- \\( t\\bar{t} \\) modelling (theory) uncertainty\n\nEach of these uncertainties is documented in the analysis, contributing to the overall systematic uncertainty of the measurement.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2604.21670 reports 12 systematic uncertainties, including diboson cross-section theoretical uncertainty, electron and muon reconstruction, identification, trigger efficiency and energy scale/resolution uncertainties, flavour tagging uncertainty, Higgs boson branching ratio uncertainty, integrated luminosity uncertainty, jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty, pile-up modelling uncertainty, single top theoretical modelling uncertainty, tau-lepton reconstruction/identification uncertainty, WW modelling uncertainty, Z+jets modelling uncertainty, and \\( t\\\\bar{t} \\\\) modelling (theory) uncertainty.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "