{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-0cacfc71", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2304.08962 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2304.08962 uses four statistical methods:\n\n1. Asymptotic profile-likelihood-ratio formula \\( Z = \\sqrt{2 \\ln \\left[\\frac{L(s_{\\text{hat}}, \\theta_{\\text{hat}})}{L(0, \\theta_{\\text{hat\\_hat}})}\\right]} \\) for significance calculation.\n2. Simultaneous signal-region/control-region likelihood with nuisance parameters constrained by Gaussian subsidiary measurements.\n3. Toy Monte Carlo studies used to exclude alternative fit models (two-resonance interfering / three-resonance non-interfering) at >95% CL relative to model A.\n4. Unbinned maximum likelihood fit to the 4mu invariant mass spectra.\n\nThese methods are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n1. \"Asymptotic profile-likelihood-ratio formula \\( Z = \\sqrt{2 \\ln \\left[\\frac{L(s_{\\text{hat}}, \\theta_{\\text{hat}})}{L(0, \\theta_{\\text{hat\\_hat}})}\\right]} \\) for significance calculation.\"\n2. \"Simultaneous signal-region/control-region likelihood with nuisance parameters constrained by Gaussian subsidiary measurements.\"\n3. \"Toy Monte Carlo studies used to exclude alternative fit models (two-resonance interfering / three-resonance non-interfering) at >95% CL relative to model A.\"\n4. \"Unbinned maximum likelihood fit to the 4mu invariant mass spectra.\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis 2304.08962 uses **4** statistical methods.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2304.08962 uses 4 statistical methods: 1. Asymptotic profile-likelihood-ratio formula \\( Z = \\\\sqrt{2 \\\\ln \\\\left[\\\\frac{L(s_{\\\\text{hat}}, \\\\theta_{\\\\text{hat}})}{L(0, \\\\theta_{\\\\text{hat\\\\_hat}})}\\\\right]} \\\\) for significance calculation. 2. Simultaneous signal-region/control-region likelihood with nuisance parameters constrained by Gaussian subsidiary measurements. 3. Toy Monte Carlo studies used to exclude alternative fit models (two-resonance interfering / three-resonance non-interfering) at >95% CL relative to model A. 4. Unbinned maximum likelihood fit to the 4mu invariant mass spectra. These methods are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper: 1. 'Asymptotic profile-likelihood-ratio formula \\( Z = \\\\sqrt{2 \\\\ln \\\\left[\\\\frac{L(s_{\\\\text{hat}}, \\\\theta_{\\\\text{hat}})}{L(0, \\\\theta_{\\\\text{hat\\\\_hat}})}\\\\right]} \\\\) for significance calculation.' 2. 'Simultaneous signal-region/control-region likelihood with nuisance parameters constrained by Gaussian subsidiary measurements.' 3. 'Toy Monte Carlo studies used to exclude alternative fit models (two-resonance interfering / three-resonance non-interfering) at >95% CL relative to model A.' 4. 'Unbinned maximum likelihood fit to the 4mu invariant mass spectra.' Therefore, the analysis 2304.08962 uses **4** statistical methods.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2304.08962"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:05a9ee2bdc4b926c32444d96", "hepkg:evidence:24f72e1f323cf0e953defcd2", "hepkg:evidence:8b7ebd7a0284234ce781c0b7", "hepkg:evidence:90de6b8d32de1d36c1fdab5c"], "seen_values": ["0", "2", "2304.08962", "4", "95", "alternative", "asymptotic", "calculation", "carlo", "constrained", "control-region", "exclude", "fit", "for", "formula", "gaussian", "interfering", "invariant", "likelihood", "mass", "maximum", "measurements", "model", "models", "monte", "non-interfering", "none", "nuisance", "parameters", "profile-likel