{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-13c5964c", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2511.11853 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2511.11853 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- **ABCD (matrix) data-driven background estimation** using control regions in data with parametric fits\n- **Asymptotic 95% CL limit setting** (CLs method)\n- **CMS Combine statistical analysis tool** (RooFit/RooStats-based)\n- **Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test** between ABCD prediction and observed data\n- **Gaussian probability density function** for shape-affecting nuisance parameters\n- **Log-normal functional fit** for background dilepton-mass shape/normalization\n- **Log-normal probability density function** for rate-affecting nuisance parameters\n- **Look-elsewhere effect correction** via MC pseudo-experiments (global significance)\n- **Simultaneous maximum likelihood fit** across data-taking years\n\nThese methods are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"ABCD (matrix) data-driven background estimation using control regions in data with parametric fits\"\n- \"Asymptotic 95% CL limit setting (CLs method)\"\n- \"CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats-based)\"\n- \"Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test between ABCD prediction and observed data\"\n- \"Gaussian probability density function for shape-affecting nuisance parameters\"\n- \"Log-normal functional fit for background dilepton-mass shape/normalization\"\n- \"Log-normal probability density function for rate-affecting nuisance parameters\"\n- \"Look-elsewhere effect correction via MC pseudo-experiments (global significance)\"\n- \"Simultaneous maximum likelihood fit across data-taking years\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2511.11853"], "value": null, "ste