{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-143ab04b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2202.08676 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2202.08676 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Conversion (Zγ) normalization uncertainty\n- DY-tt̄ process dependence uncertainty (misidentification rate)\n- Diboson jet multiplicity modeling uncertainty\n- Diboson pT modeling uncertainty\n- Electron charge misidentification uncertainty\n- Electron energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Electron/Muon reconstruction, ID, and isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale uncertainty\n- Lepton displacement efficiency uncertainty\n- Muon energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- PDF and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty\n- Pileup modeling uncertainty\n- Prompt and misidentification rate uncertainty\n- Rare background normalization uncertainty\n- Statistical uncertainty (finite MC/data sideband event counts)\n- Trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- Unclustered energy scale uncertainty\n- WZ normalization uncertainty\n- ZZ normalization uncertainty\n- b tagging efficiency uncertainty\n- τ_h energy scale uncertainty\n- τ_h reconstruction, ID, and isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- ttZ normalization uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis and reflect the various sources of systematic uncertainty considered in the study.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2401.05299", "2402