{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-147e8564", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2605.14245 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2605.14245 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- 10% nonresonant background normalization uncertainty in ggH+2jets categorization discriminants\n- Background analytic function choice uncertainty (discrete profiling)\n- Drell-Yan NLO vs LO simulation comparison shape uncertainty\n- ECAL upstream material modeling uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity and jet energy correction correlation uncertainty across data-taking years\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- NLO reweighting systematic uncertainty for VBF/VH JHUGen samples\n- Nonresonant background fit-to-data uncertainty in VH leptonic BDT distributions\n- PDF modelling uncertainty (CT14, MMHT2014 vs NNPDF3.0 replicas)\n- Per-photon energy resolution estimate uncertainty\n- Photon energy scale and resolution shape uncertainty\n- Photon identification uncertainty\n- Shower shape correction uncertainty\n- Trigger, preselection, lepton identification, MET, and pileup jet identification uncertainties\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis 2605.14245.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2605.14245 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\\n\\n- 10% nonresonant background normalization uncertainty in ggH+2jets categorization discriminants\\n- Background analytic function choice uncertainty (discrete profiling)\\n- Drell-Yan NLO vs LO simulation comparison shape uncertainty\\n- ECAL upstream material modeling uncertainty\\n- Integrated luminosity and jet energy correction correlation uncertainty across data-taking years\\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\\n- NLO reweighting syst