{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-1a4b7e48", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many quantities does analysis 2508.13900 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2508.13900 reports 23 distinct quantities. These include mass limits, upper mass reaches, and other constraints for various supersymmetric particles and processes, as well as a post-fit z-score distribution standard deviation. Each quantity is associated with specific parameters and values, such as mass differences and confidence levels.\n\nHere are some examples of the quantities reported:\n- Most stringent 95% CL lower mass limits for selectron (RR, LL, both) at Δm ~ 5 GeV: 160, 230, 250 GeV\n- Slepton masses excluded at 95% CL or higher (three chirality cases: RR-only, LL-only, both) for Δm range 3-80 GeV: 110, 175, 200 GeV\n- T2bW most stringent exclusion Δm range: 35-140 GeV\n- Post-fit z-score distribution standard deviation relative to expected unity: 1.12\n\nThese quantities provide detailed constraints on various supersymmetric models and scenarios.\n\nThe graph supports this answer with the following evidence:\n- Each quantity is linked to the analysis 2508.13900 through the `result_reports_quantity` predicate.\n\nTherefore, the answer is supported by the graph.\n\nAnswer: Analysis 2508.13900 reports 23 distinct quantities.\nAnswerable: true\nReason: answered", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2508.13900"], "predicate": "result_reports_quantity"}, "rows": 25, "error": null, "seconds": 0.051}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0d7c81827531e445d0913176", "hepkg:evidence:27a12da67bd39848d16dd0fc", "hepkg:evidence:2bdf6c94531549990adf35b5", "hepkg:evidence:377f38312f81ea45bb6362a0", "hepkg:evidence:3a1ec5eea496a92e07c0b