{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-1ca17252", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2110.11231 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2110.11231 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Full set of Section 7 systematic uncertainties included as nuisance parameters\n- ISR/FSR parton shower modelling uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale uncertainty\n- Lepton energy scale uncertainty\n- Lepton identification and isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- Nonprompt lepton background normalization and shape uncertainty\n- PDF and QCD scale (factorization/renormalization) theoretical uncertainty\n- PDF envelope (CT14, MMHT2014) uncertainty in charge asymmetry prediction\n- Pile-up modelling uncertainty\n- Statistical plus background-related uncertainty in unfolded differential distributions\n- Total unfolding uncertainty in differential cross section measurement\n- Trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- VH background normalization uncertainty\n- VVV triboson background normalization uncertainty\n- WZ EWK (VBS) background normalization uncertainty\n- b tagging efficiency uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the paper and are part of the systematic evaluation of the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2006.05880", "2110.11231", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2308.02285", "2401.05299", "2403.01556", "2503.19420", "2508.13900"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2110.11231"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 17, "error": null, "seconds": 0.046}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:b-tagging-efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:background-related-uncertainty-differential", "hepkg:systematic:charge-asymmetry