{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-204c86bf", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2004.01678 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2004.01678 uses five methods for background estimation and statistical analysis:\n\n- CLs technique\n- MC-based reweighting correction for \\( m_{\\ell\\ell j} \\)-\\( M \\) correlation\n- Maximum-likelihood fit\n- Modified ABCD estimate\n- Profile-likelihood test statistic\n\nThese methods are used to estimate backgrounds and perform statistical tests in the analysis. \n\nTo specifically address background estimation methods, the following are used:\n- MC-based reweighting correction for \\( m_{\\ell\\ell j} \\)-\\( M \\) correlation\n- Modified ABCD estimate\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses **2** background-estimation methods.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.01678"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:mc-reweighting-correction", "hepkg:method:modified-abcd-estimate", "hepkg:statistical_method:cls-technique", "hepkg:statistical_method:maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:statistical_method:profile-likelihood-test-statistic"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:7e921623cac7e5353888dbf1", "hepkg:evidence:7ecdad2b732ba2518dfa45ef", "hepkg:evidence:a0fa20300b3f0a4b999977a8"], "seen_values": ["2004.01678", "abcd", "background_method", "cls", "correction", "correlation", "estimate", "fit", "for", "hepkg:method:mc-reweighting-correction", "hepkg:method:modified-abcd-estimate", "hepkg:statistical_method:cls-technique", "hepkg:statistical_method:maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:statistical_method:profile-likelihood-test-statistic", "m_llj-m