{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-20801f04", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2012.03799 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2012.03799 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n1. **Asimov Z significance formula** for signal-region optimisation and observed excess quantification.\n2. **Background-only simultaneous likelihood fit** to control regions (CRs) and signal regions (SRs) with normalisation factors.\n3. **CLs prescription** for exclusion limit setting.\n4. **Profile-likelihood-ratio test** for the background-only hypothesis (p0, Z significance).\n\nThese methods are documented in the paper with the following verbatim quotes:\n\n- Asimov Z significance formula: \"Asimov Z significance formula for signal-region optimisation and observed excess quantification.\"\n- Background-only simultaneous likelihood fit: \"Background-only simultaneous likelihood fit to CRs (and SRs) with normalisation factors.\"\n- CLs prescription: \"CLs prescription for exclusion limit setting.\"\n- Profile-likelihood-ratio test: \"Profile-likelihood-ratio test for background-only hypothesis (p0, Z significance).\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2012.03799"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2012.03799"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:statmethod:background-only-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:statmethod:cls-prescription", "hepkg:statmethod:profile-likelihood-ratio-test", "hepkg:statmethod:z-significance"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:2e6cd8abc148c4d23d5d0009", "hepkg:evidence:4670a83ce1edbb2a7f4ab411", "hepkg:evidence:735214fde14f5231f872cdc8", "hepkg:evidence:77fabef1b139adf90524feee", "hepkg:evidence:c