{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-216dfdf5", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2510.07527 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2510.07527 reports 22 distinct systematic uncertainties. Here they are:\n\n- Dedicated uncorrelated uncertainties from data-driven background estimation methods\n- ECAL first-level trigger timing inefficiency correction/normalisation uncertainty (2016-2017)\n- Electroweak correction uncertainties for ttZ, ttW, qqZZ, and ggZZ processes\n- HCAL 2018 two-module-off correction and associated shape uncertainty\n- Higgs boson branching fraction theoretical uncertainties (1.2% bb, 1.5% WW/ZZ, 2.1% gamgam, 1.6% tautau)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Jet flavour (b-tagging) discriminant shape nuisance parameters\n- Jet selection efficiency shape uncertainty\n- Muon, electron, and tau_h identification efficiency correction uncertainty\n- PDF uncertainty (3%) on ggF HH cross section\n- PYTHIA colour-correlated recoil scale uncertainty\n- Parton shower ISR/FSR, top quark mass, and renormalisation/factorisation scale uncertainties for ttbar and single top production\n- Photon identification efficiency shape uncertainty\n- Pileup modelling uncertainty from inelastic pp cross section (4.6%) and pileup distribution shape\n- Renormalisation/factorisation scale, alpha_S, and PDF uncertainties on simulated process cross sections\n- Theoretical uncertainty on nonresonant ggF HH cross section as a function of kappa_lambda (scales + top mass, -23%/+6% at SM point)\n- Trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- Uncertainty in rate of Higgs boson production associated with heavy-flavour jets (50%)\n- Unclustered energy reconstruction uncertainty affecting pT^miss shape\n- VBF HH production theoretical uncertainties (scales +0.03%/-0.04%, PDF+alphaS 2.1%)\n- ttbar NNLO top quark pT reweighting shape uncertainty\n\nEach of these uncertainties is documented in the analysis, contributing to the overall systematic uncertainty budget.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2604.21670", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2510.07527"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 22, "error": null, "seconds": 0.049}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:data_driven_bkg_method_uncertainty", "hepkg:systematic:ecal_l1_trigger_timing_2016_2017", "hepkg:systematic:ew_corrections_ttz_ttw_qqzz_ggzz", "hepkg:systematic:ggf_hh_pdf_3pct", "hepkg:systematic:ggf_hh_theory_xs_kappa_lambda", "hepkg:systematic:hcal_2018_module_off", "hepkg:systematic:heavy_flavour_jet_rate", "hepkg:systematic:higgs_branching_fraction", "hepkg:systematic:isr_fsr_topmass_scale_ttbar_singletop", "hepkg:systematic:jet_energy_scale_resolution", "hepkg:systematic:jet_flavour_discriminant_shape", "hepkg:systematic:jet_selection_efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:lepton_tauh_id_efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:luminosity", "hepkg:systematic:photon_id_efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:pileup_inelastic_xs", "hepkg:systematic:pythia_colour_correlated_recoil", "hepkg:systematic:theory_scale_pdf_alphas", "hepkg:systematic:trigger_efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:ttbar_nnlo_pt_reweighting", "hepkg:systematic:unclustered_energy_met", "hepkg:systematic:vbf_hh_theory_xs"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:06702ffe2cd3c423bb313b00", "hepkg:evidence:0773e8f2731e6d1b5c5d75f9", "he