{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-22811c51", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2510.07527 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2510.07527 uses four statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n1. Asymptotic profile likelihood ratio test statistic -2Δln(L) with CLs criterion\n2. Barlow-Beeston approach for MC statistical uncertainties in the likelihood\n3. CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats frameworks)\n4. Global (statistically combined) maximum likelihood fit across analyses\n\nThese methods are used to estimate the background in the analysis. \n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2510.07527 uses four statistical methods for background estimation:\\n\\n1. Asymptotic profile likelihood ratio test statistic -2Δln(L) with CLs criterion\\n2. Barlow-Beeston approach for MC statistical uncertainties in the likelihood\\n3. CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats frameworks)\\n4. Global (statistically combined) maximum likelihood fit across analyses\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.14246", "2510.07527"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2510.07527"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.035}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:statmethod:barlow_beeston", "hepkg:statmethod:combine_roofit_roostats", "hepkg:statmethod:global_ml_fit", "hepkg:statmethod:profile_likelihood_asymptotic_cls"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:45799591c5678819809a38e9", "hepkg:evidence:558c565c896955ed045a47a9", "hepkg:evidence:865f61aab89ce5d64c860c3c", "hepkg:evidence:c391f2b439b26cb0cccd4f11"], "seen_valu