{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-2407bbfa", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2112.03161 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2112.03161 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- **2D binned maximum likelihood fit** of \\( m_{bb} \\) and \\( m_{HH} \\) distributions\n- **Asymptotic approximation of the CLs method** for 95% CL upper limits\n- **Likelihood ratio goodness-of-fit test** using the saturated model\n- **Pseudo-experiments** used to validate asymptotic limit calculation and test signal-fit bias\n\nThese methods are detailed in the paper and are used to estimate and validate the background in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.03161", "2201.11585"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2112.03161"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cls_asymptotic", "hepkg:method:goodness_of_fit_saturated", "hepkg:method:ml_fit_2d", "hepkg:method:pseudoexperiments_crosscheck"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:05c964f0b33167be71d5b7a8", "hepkg:evidence:7dd38e4b699ab3ee943162be", "hepkg:evidence:8b6262f4d7c09fcccd20764c", "hepkg:evidence:bfb3c17c2721c5db0f15c18c", "hepkg:evidence:e1682016e18285e291d29717"], "seen_values": ["2", "2112.03161", "95", "and", "approximation", "asymptotic", "bias", "binned", "calculation", "cls", "distributions", "fit", "for", "goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:method:cls_asymptotic", "hepkg:method:goodness_of_fit_saturated", "hepkg:method:ml_fit_2d", "hepkg:method:pseudoexperiments_crosscheck", "likelihood", "limit", "limits", "m_bb", "m_hh", "maximum", "method", "model", "pseudo-experiments", "ratio", "result_uses_statistical_method", "saturated", "signal-fit", "st