{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-2783c6c8", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2604.27044 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2604.27044 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Barlow-Beeston lite technique for binwise statistical uncertainty modeling\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for SUSY signal strength, background yields and nuisance parameters\n- CMS statistical analysis tool Combine (RooFit/RooStats based)\n- Feldman-Cousins (FC) procedure for coupling modifier interval coverage\n- Fisher F-test for polynomial/basis-function order selection\n- Modified frequentist CLs criterion with asymptotic approximation\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic\n- Quantile matching procedure for validation region input feature alignment\n- Saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test\n- Wilks' theorem asymptotic interpretation of profiled likelihood test statistic\n- k-fold ensembling method for background reweighting DNN variance estimation\n\nThese methods are documented in the analysis paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2009.04363", "2107.12553", "2209.07327", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.27044"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.039}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow-beeston-lite", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-modified-frequentist", "hepkg:method:combine-tool", "hepkg:method:feldman-cousins", "hepkg:method:fisher-f-test", "hepkg:method:k-fold-ensembling", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-ratio", "hepkg:method:quantile-matching", "hepkg:method:saturated-chi2-gof", "hepkg:method:wilks-theorem"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:25b18e888c4e90f56dcef547", "hepkg:evidence:3a15e120794603923eefbcc