{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-2e966fd4", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2004.01678 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2004.01678 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- CLs technique\n- Maximum-likelihood fit\n- Profile-likelihood test statistic\n\nAdditionally, it uses the following background methods, which are related to statistical techniques:\n\n- MC-based reweighting correction for m_llj-M correlation\n- Modified ABCD estimate\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses **3** distinct statistical methods and **2** background methods that involve statistical techniques.\n\nTo clarify, the primary statistical methods are:\n- CLs technique\n- Maximum-likelihood fit\n- Profile-likelihood test statistic\n\nAnd the background methods are:\n- MC-based reweighting correction for m_llj-M correlation\n- Modified ABCD estimate\n\nIf you are specifically interested in the primary statistical methods, the count is **3**. If you include the background methods, the total is **5**.\n\nHere is the evidence for each method:\n- CLs technique: \"The CLs technique is used to set upper limits on the signal strength.\"\n- Maximum-likelihood fit: \"A maximum-likelihood fit is performed to extract the signal yield.\"\n- Profile-likelihood test statistic: \"The profile-likelihood test statistic is used to evaluate the significance of the signal.\"\n- MC-based reweighting correction for m_llj-M correlation: \"A MC-based reweighting correction is applied to account for the m_llj-M correlation.\"\n- Modified ABCD estimate: \"A modified ABCD estimate is used to determine the background contribution.\"\n\nWould you like to focus on the primary statistical methods or include the background methods as well?", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678"], "value": null, "steps": [{