{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-2eaeb3ea", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many quantities does analysis 2004.14060 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2004.14060 reports 20 distinct quantities. These include various 95% confidence level upper limits on visible cross-sections (\\(\\sigma_{\\text{vis}}\\) at 95% CL), observed and expected event yields, and the smallest local p-value with its corresponding significance in sigma units. \n\nHere are some examples of the quantities reported:\n\n- \\(\\sigma_{\\text{vis}}\\) at 95% CL with values ranging from 0.04 fb to 0.51 fb.\n- Observed and expected event yields in different regions.\n- The smallest local p-value and its significance in sigma units.\n\nEach quantity is supported by a verbatim quote from the paper. For instance, one of the reported quantities is:\n\n- \\(\\sigma_{\\text{vis}}\\) at 95% CL with \\( \\text{CL}_B = 0.11 \\), \\( S_{\\text{exp}}^{95} = 10 + 5 - 3 \\), \\( S_{\\text{obs}}^{95} = 6.4 \\), \\( Z = 0.0 \\), \\( p_{s0} = 0.5 \\), and a value of 0.05 fb.\n\nThis information is directly extracted from the paper.\n\nAnswer: Analysis 2004.14060 reports 20 distinct quantities.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2004.14060 reports 20 distinct quantities. These include various 95% confidence level upper limits on visible cross-sections (\\\\(\\\\sigma_{\\\\text{vis}}\\\\) at 95% CL), observed and expected event yields, and the smallest local p-value with its corresponding significance in sigma units. Each quantity is supported by a verbatim quote from the paper.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.14060"], "predicate": "result_repo