{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-34ffe27b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many collision systems does analysis 2604.21670 study?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2604.21670 studies two collision systems:\n\n1. \\( e^+e^- \\) collisions at the Z pole (LEP/SLD)\n2. Proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s} = 13 \\) TeV\n\nThese details are supported by the following entries in the graph:\n\n- For \\( e^+e^- \\) collisions at the Z pole: \"e+e- collisions at the Z pole (LEP/SLD)\"\n- For proton-proton collisions at \\( \\sqrt{s} = 13 \\) TeV: \"proton-proton collisions at sqrt(s) = 13 TeV\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis 2604.21670 studies **two** collision systems.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2604.21670 studies two collision systems: \\( e^+e^- \\) collisions at the Z pole (LEP/SLD) and proton-proton collisions at \\( \\\\sqrt{s} = 13 \\\\) TeV.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2007.02873", "2012.08600", "2103.04956", "2106.14246", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2207.12246", "2208.12095", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2309.14442", "2401.07090", "2509.22535", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.21670"], "predicate": "result_has_collision_system"}, "rows": 2, "error": null, "seconds": 0.018}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:collision_system:ee_zpole", "hepkg:collision_system:pp_13tev"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:6cab492a76ec0b1d39a7cdab", "hepkg:evidence:b015c1aedc380b525b109d52"], "seen_values": ["13", "2604.2167", "2604.21670", "collision_system", "collisions", "hepkg:collision_system:ee_zpole", "hepkg:collision_system:pp_13tev", "lep", "pole", "prot