{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-36443869", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2207.00348 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2207.00348 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Asimov data set for expected results\n- CL$_{s}$ method for exclusion\n- Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test of background template\n- Gaussian-kernel template smoothing (background method)\n- Gaussian/log-normal nuisance-parameter constraint pdfs in likelihood\n- Maximum-likelihood fit to data\n- Principal component analysis of the SMEFT information matrix\n- Profile likelihood technique for CL intervals\n- Pseudo-experiments drawn from background template to validate chi2 p-values\n- Spurious-signal test for background function selection (background method)\n- Wald test for background-function selection\n\nThese methods are used to analyze the data and draw conclusions from the analysis.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2207.00348", "2307.01094"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2207.00348"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:gaussian-kernel-smoothing", "hepkg:method:spurious-signal-test", "hepkg:statmethod:asimov-dataset", "hepkg:statmethod:chi2-goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:statmethod:cls-method", "hepkg:statmethod:maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:statmethod:nuisance-parameter-constraints", "hepkg:statmethod:principal-component-analysis", "hepkg:statmethod:profile-likelihood", "hepkg:statmethod:pseudo-experiments-bootstrap", "hepkg:statmethod:wald-test"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0257f5ec1f3d25a3b1d67ce6", "hepkg:evidence:1cc6d9b08b9f25690a93b25c", "hepkg:evidence:295087a09c1bbc5729f1b8ad", "hepkg:ev