{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-3b05c6bb", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2207.12246 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2207.12246 reports 22 systematic uncertainties, including:\n\n- ALFA detector spatial resolution uncertainty\n- Background subtraction uncertainty (accidental coincidences and DPE)\n- Beam emittance model uncertainty\n- Beam transport method uncertainty (PTC-tracking vs transport-matrix simulation)\n- Coulomb phase parameterization uncertainty\n- Detector alignment systematic uncertainty (distance, offsets, rotation)\n- Effective beam optics model uncertainty (Q1,Q3,Q5,Q6 vs Q5,Q6-only fit)\n- Event reconstruction efficiency uncertainty (incl. t-dependence)\n- LHC beam energy uncertainty\n- Luminosity calibration-transfer (vdM-to-high-beta* regime) uncertainty\n- Luminosity long-term stability uncertainty\n- Luminosity single-beam background uncertainty\n- Proton electric form-factor parameterization uncertainty\n- Residual LHC crossing-angle uncertainty\n- Spin-dependent (magnetic-moment) Coulomb amplitude uncertainty\n- Theoretical nuclear-amplitude slope-model choice uncertainty (BCD/BC/B)\n- Total integrated luminosity systematic uncertainty\n- Track reconstruction fibre-layer requirement uncertainty (3 vs 4 layers)\n- Unfolding closure-test (data-driven bias) uncertainty\n- rho-parameter input variation in simulation\n- t-dependent nuclear phase model uncertainty\n- t-spectrum slope model uncertainty (BCD vs constant-B simulation)\n- vdM absolute luminosity calibration uncertainty\n\nEach of these uncertainties is documented in the analysis, contributing to the overall systematic uncertainty of the measurement.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2207.12246 reports 22 systematic uncertainties, including various sources such as detector resolution, background subtraction, beam emittance, and more. Each of these uncertainties is documented in the analysis, contributing to the overall systematic uncertainty of the measurement.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2207.12246", "2303.15340"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2207.12246"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 23, "error": null, "seconds": 0.049}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:alignment", "hepkg:systematic:background_subtraction", "hepkg:systematic:beam_energy", "hepkg:systematic:beam_optics", "hepkg:systematic:beam_transport_ptc", "hepkg:systematic:crossing_angle", "hepkg:systematic:detector_resolution", "hepkg:systematic:emittance_model", "hepkg:systematic:luminosity_background", "hepkg:systematic:luminosity_calibration_transfer", "hepkg:systematic:luminosity_long_term_stability", "hepkg:systematic:luminosity_total", "hepkg:systematic:luminosity_vdm_calibration", "hepkg:systematic:reconstruction_efficiency_unc", "hepkg:systematic:rho_variation", "hepkg:systematic:simulation_slope_model", "hepkg:systematic:theory_coulomb_phase", "hepkg:systematic:theory_form_factor", "hepkg:systematic:theory_nuclear_phase_model", "hepkg:systematic:theory_slope_model_choice", "hepkg:systematic:theory_spin_dependence", "hepkg:systematic:tracking_efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:unfolding_closure"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:017e7f921f18f62fbf2cb0b8", "hepkg:evidence:06535ff1b88dee3ba41f3430", "hepkg:evidence:0668544f829a1f4ec37cfe91", "hepkg:evidence:1322b4b5fa5202ff28ebe138", "hepkg:evidence:43c9a6bad0fa30fea8de8b1b", "hepkg:evidence:447b226a8cb58bb4a525213f", "hepkg:evidence:489a8fde856bd3273bf424d7", "hepkg:evidence:5a4b329068cda34ed5f6bb34", "hepkg:evidence:65a2c62bb9e774cf09411262", "hepkg:evidence:6c312b83f665cb3b4259a67c", "hepkg:evidence:8f362a3b27b4