{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-407de045", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2408.03744 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2408.03744 defines 16 object selection requirements. These include criteria for jet algorithms, lepton \\( p_T \\) thresholds, isolation requirements, and other kinematic selections.\n\nHere are some examples:\n- Jet algorithm: anti-\\( k_T \\) with distance parameter 0.4, input: particle-flow candidates.\n- Lepton \\( p_T \\) thresholds: \n  - \\( p_T > 25 \\) GeV for \\( W \\) boson fiducial region signal leptons.\n  - \\( p_T > 25 \\) GeV for \\( Z \\) boson fiducial region leptons.\n  - \\( p_T > 17 \\) GeV for trigger leptons.\n- Additional lepton veto: \\( p_T > 10 \\) GeV.\n- Dilepton invariant mass window: \\( 60 < m_{ll} < 120 \\) GeV.\n- Isolation cone radius: 0.3 and 0.4.\n- Quality requirements on the number of spatial measurements in the silicon tracker and muon system.\n\nThese selections ensure that the analysis focuses on the desired physics processes and reduces backgrounds.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2408.03744 defines 16 object selection requirements. These include criteria for jet algorithms, lepton \\( p_T \\) thresholds, isolation requirements, and other kinematic selections.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 16, "error": null, "seconds": 0.04}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:038d4e87a1ef72318965575b", "hepkg:evidence:10301b89ff017a7d476a1861", "hepkg:evidence:1cf38a87896b982d7dfe8e23", "hepkg:evidence:1e7935