{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-4413ef4e", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2604.27044 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2604.27044 reports 19 systematic uncertainties. Here they are:\n\n1. Background prediction extrapolation bias uncertainty (CR mass sideband to SR)\n2. Background prediction shape uncertainty parameterized via Fourier basis functions\n3. Background prediction statistical variance uncertainty from finite CR/SR data and k-fold model spread\n4. GloParT X->bb tagging efficiency scale factor uncertainty (10-25%)\n5. H->bb branching fraction theoretical uncertainty (2.5%)\n6. HH signal acceptance theoretical uncertainty (NNPDF parameters, muR/muF scale factor 2/0.5, parton shower ISR/FSR)\n7. Jet energy scale (JES) and jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n8. Jet mass scale (JMS) and resolution (JMR) uncertainty for H->bb candidate AK8 jets\n9. PDF set choice uncertainty on inclusive ggHH cross section (±1.5%)\n10. Post-regression AK4 jet pT scale (1-2%) and resolution (4-8%) uncertainty\n11. QCD muR/muF scale variation uncertainty on ggHH cross section (+2.1%,-4.9%)\n12. QCD multijet background normalization uncertainty from unconstrained transfer factor profiling (merged, alphabet method)\n13. Top quark mass value/definition (scheme) uncertainty on ggHH cross section (+4%,-18%)\n14. Trigger efficiency scale factor, integrated luminosity, and pileup modeling uncertainty\n15. alpha_S uncertainty on ggHH cross section (±1.7%)\n16. b jet tagging efficiency and light-flavor misidentification rate uncertainty\n17. qqHH inclusive cross section PDF and alpha_S uncertainty (±2.7%)\n18. qqHH inclusive cross section QCD scale variation uncertainty (+0.05%,-0.03%)\n19. ttbar background correction uncertainties (T_Xbb tagging score, tau32, recoil pT(jj)) in merged analysis\n\nThis list is based on the systematic uncertainties explicitly recorded in the graph for this analysis. Each uncertainty is supported by a verbatim quote from the paper.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.01676", "2209.07327", "2308.02285", "2407.10549", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.27044"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 19, "error": null, "seconds": 0.048}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:background-extrapolation-bias", "hepkg:systematic:background-shape-fourier", "hepkg:systematic:background-variance-kfold", "hepkg:systematic:bbtag-efficiency-sf", "hepkg:systematic:btag-efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-alphas", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-pdf", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-qcd-scale", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-topmass", "hepkg:systematic:hbb-brfrac", "hepkg:systematic:jes-jer", "hepkg:systematic:jetpt-regression-scale-resolution", "hepkg:systematic:jms-jmr", "hepkg:systematic:qcd-multijet-normalization-merged", "hepkg:systematic:qqhh-pdf-alphas", "hepkg:systematic:qqhh-qcdscale", "hepkg:systematic:signal-acceptance-theory", "hepkg:systematic:trigger-lumi-pileup", "hepkg:systematic:ttbar-correction-merged"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1d47cbb62109d0c66317c0d6", "hepkg:evidence:23c8532339d8e2e1ebd57a7b", "hepkg:evidence:36f7fdae160472d9764cbd5f", "hepkg:evidence:3704bc9cedde6ce7b57bbe05", "hepkg:evidence:37061f7a08aee642010f5e24", "hepkg:evidence:3c2ae45ce594da595d6e761e", "hepkg:evidence:59e0d5481bd66c42bdee1814", "hepkg:evidence:6add3537d12652f3fb36d10c", "hepkg:evidence:8aa8ba2ac07cf0cb33602f70", "hepkg:evidence:9cc96e64cc1a6c546c56828f", "hepkg:evidence:a39f08a8fd357caee527c0ff", "hepkg:evidence:c9d72f09bc3bc9f71cffadd1", "hepkg:evidence:d0ddae70a74efd378f825c81", "hepkg:evidence:e9f5d0945685c00fbacb7246", "hepkg:evidence:f665b938b57e77f88c208ea3", "hepkg:evidence:f7f895201ac6cfba32c2a548"], "se