{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-46293488", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2602.18611 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2602.18611 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- **Asimov data set method for expected results**\n- **Asymptotic approximation for 68%/95% CL intervals (q<1, q<3.84; q<2.30, q<5.99 for 2D)**\n- **Barlow-Beeston lite approach for MC statistical uncertainties in simulated templates**\n- **CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats)**\n- **Correlation matrix extraction from second derivatives of q(alpha) around best fit**\n- **Maximum likelihood fits to extract SMEFT Wilson coefficient constraints**\n- **Moment matching procedure to determine simplified-likelihood parameters (dimidated Gaussian)**\n- **Principal component analysis (PCA) of Hessian matrix to derive constrained SMEFT eigenvector directions**\n- **Profile likelihood ratio test statistic q(alpha)**\n- **SM compatibility p-value from chi-square distribution of q(alpha_SM)**\n- **Simplified likelihood procedure (Gaussian/dimidated-Gaussian approximation) for SMEFT constraints**\n\nThese methods are used for various aspects of the statistical analysis, including background estimation, likelihood fitting, and hypothesis testing.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2602.18611"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2602.18611"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow_beeston_lite", "hepkg:statistical_method:asimov_dataset_method", "hepkg:statistical_method:asymptotic_approximation_cl_intervals", "hepkg:statistical_method:combine_roofit_roostats_tool", "hepkg:statistical_method:hessian_correlation_e