{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-4d1cd1ab", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2004.14060 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2004.14060 measures the following observables:\n\n- 95% CL upper limit on the number of BSM signal events (S_obs^95, S_exp^95)\n- 95% CL upper limit on the visible BSM cross section (σ_vis = ⟨εσ⟩_obs^95)\n- Discovery p-value p(s=0) and local significance (Z) for the background-only hypothesis\n\nThese measurements are supported by the following quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"95% CL upper limit on number of BSM signal events (S_obs^95, S_exp^95)\"\n- \"95% CL upper limit on visible BSM cross section (\\\\sigma_{vis} = \\\\langle\\\\epsilon\\\\sigma\\\\rangle_{obs}^{95})\"\n- \"Discovery p-value p(s=0) and local significance (Z) for background-only hypothesis\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2004.14060 measures the following observables:\\n\\n- 95% CL upper limit on the number of BSM signal events (S_obs^95, S_exp^95)\\n- 95% CL upper limit on the visible BSM cross section (σ_vis = ⟨εσ⟩_obs^95)\\n- Discovery p-value p(s=0) and local significance (Z) for the background-only hypothesis\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.14060"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:local_significance", "hepkg:observable:signal_event_limit", "hepkg:observable:visible_cross_section_limit"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:3b06056588fb280a99cd14e9", "hepkg:evidence:49ddfdb21badebb3414b057d", "hepkg:evidence:4b67c7b32d335f52e2316ff7"], "seen_values": ["0", "2004.1406", "2004.14060", "95", "and", "background-only", "bsm", "cross", "discovery", "epsilon", "events", "for", "hepkg:observable:local_significance", "hepkg:observable:signal_event_limit", "hepkg:observable:visible_cross_section_limit", "hypothesis", "langle", "limit", "local", "number", "obs", "observable", "p-value", "rangle_", "result_measures_observable", "s_exp", "s_obs", "section", "sigma", "sigma_", "signal", "significance", "upper", "vis", "visible"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 8898, "completion_tokens": 373, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 16.870005500968546, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 16.870005500968546, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9271.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 3.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 1.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 3.0, "evidence_quotes": 3.0}}
{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-4d227ce9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2209.07327 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2209.07327 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Barlow-Beeston method for simulated-sample statistical uncertainties\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for SUSY signal strength, background yields and nuisance parameters\n- CLs method for limit setting\n- Chi-square minimization of lepton pT distributions for nonprompt rate determination\n- Lognormal-distributed nuisance parameters for normalization-only systematic uncertainties\n- Profile likelihood test statistic in the asymptotic approximation\n- Saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test\n- Template morphing with Gaussian probability distributions for shape systematics\n\nThese methods are documented in the paper with the arXiv ID 2209.07327.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2209.07327 uses the following statistical methods:\\n\\n- Barlow-Beeston method for simulated-sample statistical uncertainties\\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for SUSY signal strength, background yields and nuisance parameters\\n- CLs method for limit setting\\n- Chi-square minimization of lepton pT distributions for nonprompt rate determination\\n- Lognormal-distributed nuisance parameters for normalization-only systematic uncertainties\\n- Profile likelihood test statistic in the asymptotic approximation\\n- Saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test\\n- Template morphing with Gaussian probability distributions for shape systematics\\n\\nThese methods are documented in the paper with the arXiv ID 2209.07327.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2107.12553", "2209.07327", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2209.07327"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 8, "error": null, "seconds": 0.039}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow-beeston", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:chi2-minimization-nonprompt", "hepkg:method:cls", "hepkg:method:lognormal-nuisance", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-asymptotic", "hepkg:method:saturated-chi2-gof", "hepkg:method:template-morphing"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:46ae61373b5cc23fb820f62e", "hepkg:evidence:496ee2532d23d4dfaee8e2ff", "hepkg:evidence:565d4bb176b0c84d07f01e1f", "hepkg:evidence:57852945fec9725c9113eee6", "hepkg:evidence:66218aa2a52d0e5c0ec828dc", "hepkg:evidence:a4abb615ea03bd2038c75444", "hepkg:evidence:ba5404d92fe32e4627d852ed"], "seen_values": ["2209.07327", "and", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "barlow-beeston", "binned", "chi-square", "cls", "determination", "distributions", "fit", "for", "gaussian", "goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:method:barlow-beeston", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:chi2-minimization-nonprompt", "hepkg:method:cls", "hepkg:method:lognormal-nuisance", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-asymptotic", "hepkg:method:saturated-chi2-gof", "hepkg:method:template-morphing", "lepton", "likelihood", "limit", "lognormal-distributed", "maximum", "method", "minimization", "morphing", "nonprompt", "normalization-only", "nuisance", "parameters", "probability", "profile", "rate", "result_uses_statistical_method", "saturated", "setting", "shape", "signal", "simulated-sample", "statistic", "statistical", "statistical_method", "strength", "susy", "systematic", "systematics", "template", "test", "the", "uncertainties", "with", "yields"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 9209, "completion_tokens": 368, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 13.380016815382987, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 13.380016815382987, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9577.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 8.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 1.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 8.0, "evidence_quotes": 7.0}}
{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-4d32e9aa", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2001.06899 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2001.06899 defines 10 object selection requirements. Here they are:\n\n1. Jet with \\( p_T > 30 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\) identified via HF tagging (CSVv2, medium operating point, ~10% c-jet tagging efficiency, 1% light-jet mistag), matched to a generated c hadron and not a b hadron.\n2. Jet with \\( p_T > 30 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\) identified via HF tagging (CSVv2, medium operating point, ~60% b-jet tagging efficiency, 1% light-jet mistag), matched to a generated b hadron.\n3. Opposite-charge, same-flavor lepton pair with \\( 71 < m_{ll} < 111 \\) GeV.\n4. \\( p_T > 25 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\); isolation < 25% of lepton \\( p_T \\); \\( | d_{xy} | < 0.05 \\) cm, \\( | d_z | < 0.2 \\) cm; exactly two same-flavor electrons required.\n5. \\( p_T > 25 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\); isolation < 25% of lepton \\( p_T \\); \\( | d_{xy} | < 0.05 \\) cm, \\( | d_z | < 0.2 \\) cm; exactly two same-flavor muons required.\n6. \\( p_T > 30 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\); at least one such jet required per event.\n7. \\( p_T^{\\text{miss}} < 40 \\) GeV.\n8. Stable Z-decay leptons dressed with photons within \\( \\Delta R < 0.1 \\); fiducial requirement \\( p_T > 25 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\) and \\( 71 < m_{ll} < 111 \\) GeV (same as reconstructed leptons).\n9. Stable particles (c*tau > 1 cm) except neutrinos and overlapping Z-decay leptons, clustered with anti-kT R=0.4; fiducial requirement \\( p_T > 30 \\) GeV, \\( | \\eta | < 2.4 \\) (same as reconstructed jets).\n\nThese selections are detailed in the paper and are used to define the objects and events considered in the analysis.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2001.06899 defines 10 object selection requirements. These include criteria for jets, leptons, and missing transverse energy, among others.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2001.06899"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 9, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0dad6f68b66135bf79647258", "hepkg:evidence:135db9c378c3b70e5621c664", "hepkg:evidence:254498640c811103860acbd2", "hepkg:evidence:4ba63a5408af5a22460e12a9", "hepkg:evidence:6d51c63569d1c35d180a72f4", "hepkg:evidence:82fdd12cbe491986571e78b3", "hepkg:evidence:85635c5229d4115850bd8d47", "hepkg:evidence:94694d509f2b9c7539b50243", "hepkg:evidence:ba6af461b8444b547387f75c", "hepkg:evidence:d120d0bf56cc5699c67d77b2", "hepkg:evidence:f67dd9244055263d19bfe1ac"], "seen_values": ["0.05", "0.1", "0.2", "0.4", "1", "10", "111", "2.4", "2001.06899", "25", "3", "30", "4", "40", "6", "60", "71", "and", "anti-kt", "b-jet", "c-jet", "clustered", "csvv2", "d_xy", "d_z", "deltar", "dressed", "efficiency", "electrons", "eta", "event", "exactly", "except", "fiducial", "generated", "gev", "hadron", "identified", "isolation", "jet", "jets", "least", "lepton", "leptons", "light-jet", "m_ll", "matched", "medium", "miss", "mistag", "muons", "neutrinos", "none", "not", "object_has_selection", "one", "operating", "opposite-charge", "overlapping", "p_t", "pair", "particles", "per", "photons", "point", "reconstructed", "required", "requirement", "same", "same-flavor", "stable", "such", "tagging", "tau", "two", "via", "with", "within", "z-decay"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 9449, "completion_tokens": 690, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 27.488223706837744, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 27.488223706837744, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 10139.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 0.0, "evidence_quotes": 11.0}}
