{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-4e866796", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2407.10549 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2407.10549 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n1. Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)\n2. Modified frequentist CL$_s$ approach with profile-likelihood test statistic in the asymptotic approximation\n3. Simultaneous binned maximum-likelihood fit to SR $m_{bb}$ distributions and CR event yields with free-floating background normalizations and Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2010.14293", "2106.01676", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2407.10549"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:background-only-fit", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit-simultaneous", "hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood-asymptotic"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:11aef175783c533f2b117f47", "hepkg:evidence:6e129b7c02850bfa009a490b", "hepkg:evidence:7609dffe1181e5bef124b319", "hepkg:evidence:80f1039d8b6600c1e36df7fb", "hepkg:evidence:da561d241963e7a6ded9d521"], "seen_values": ["2407.10549", "and", "approach", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "background-only", "binned", "crs", "distributions", "event", "fit", "floating", "free-floating", "frequentist", "gaussian-constrained", "hepkg:method:background-only-fit", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit-simultaneous", "hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood-asymptotic", "maximum-likelihood", "modified", "normalisation", "normalizations", "nuisance", "only", "parameters", "profile-likelihood", "result_uses_statistical_method", "signal", "simultaneous", "statistic", "statistical_method", "test", "the", "with", "yields"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 8918, "completion_tokens": 287, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 12.063271967694163, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 12.063271967694163, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9205.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 3.0, "evidence_quotes": 5.0}}
{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-4ed9cf04", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which detector objects does analysis 2006.05880 define?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2006.05880 defines the following detector objects:\n\n- Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\n- Control region CR^Z_ttZ for ttZ background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\n- Control region CR^h_ttbar for ttbar background normalisation (1ℓ selection)\n- Shape-fit signal region SR^h_1AB overlapping SR^h_1A and SR^h_1B\n- Signal region SR^Z_1A (3ℓ selection, t̃1→tχ̃2⁰ with χ̃2⁰→h/Zχ̃1⁰, large mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^Z_1B (3ℓ selection, small χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^Z_2A (3ℓ selection, t̃2→Zt̃1, small mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^Z_2B (3ℓ selection, t̃2→Zt̃1, large mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^h_1A (1ℓ selection, small χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^h_1B (1ℓ selection, large χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\n- Validation region VR^Z_1F for fake/non-prompt lepton background\n- Validation region VR^Z_2F for fake/non-prompt lepton background (soft lepton regime)\n- Validation region VR^Z_ttZ for ttZ background estimate\n- Validation region VR^{Z,b-tag}_VV for multi-boson background (b-tag veto released)\n- Validation region VR^{Z,n-jet}_VV for multi-boson background (jet multiplicity extrapolation)\n\nThese regions are used for various purposes, including background normalization, signal region definition, and validation of background estimates.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2006.05880"], "predicate": "result_defines_object"}, "rows": 15, "error": null, "seconds": 0.044}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:object:CR-Z-VV", "hepkg:object:CR-Z-ttZ", "he