{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-5252cb5b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2307.01094 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2307.01094 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ scale/resolution and soft-term uncertainty\n- 50% overall cross-section uncertainty assigned to rarer background processes not computed in detail\n- Charge-flip electron background prediction uncertainty (~50% typical, from $\\gamma$ correction measurement)\n- Fake/non-prompt lepton estimate systematic uncertainty (matrix-method $\\varepsilon$/$\\zeta$ extrapolation and contamination)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet uncertainties: JVT, jet energy scale (JES), jet energy resolution (JER), flavour tagging\n- Lepton reconstruction/identification/isolation/energy-scale/resolution/trigger efficiency uncertainties\n- Limited MC simulation sample-size statistical uncertainty\n- Pileup modeling uncertainty\n- Theoretical modelling uncertainties: renormalisation/factorisation/resummation/merging scales, PDF choice (MMHT2014, CT14, NNPDF), and cross-section normalisation\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the paper with the corresponding descriptions.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2307.01094 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\\n\\n- $E_{\\\\text{T}}^{\\\\text{miss}}$ scale/resolution and soft-term uncertainty\\n- 50% overall cross-section uncertainty assigned to rarer background processes not computed in detail\\n- Charge-flip electron background prediction uncertainty (~50% typical, from $\\\\gamma$ correction measurement)\\n- Fake/non-prompt lepton estimate systematic uncertainty (matrix-method $\\\\varepsilon$/$\\\\zeta$ extrapolation and contamination)\\n- Int