{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-54203f21", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2407.10549 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2407.10549 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $E_T^{miss}$ trigger efficiency, energy scale and resolution uncertainty (found negligible)\n- $V\\!+\\!\\mathrm{jets}$ matching parameter and resummation scale uncertainty\n- $V\\!+\\!\\mathrm{jets}$ normalization uncertainty\n- $Z\\!+\\!\\mathrm{jets}$ modeling uncertainty\n- $b$-jet identification algorithm calibration uncertainty\n- $tW$ channel interference with $t\\bar{t}$ production uncertainty (diagram subtraction scheme)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) and jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet mass scale (JMS) uncertainty for large-$R$ jets\n- Lepton identification efficiency uncertainty (found negligible)\n- Matrix element and parton shower generator choice uncertainty\n- PDF choice and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis as part of the systematic evaluation.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2510.07527", "2604.21670", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2407.10549"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 12, "error": null, "seconds": 0.046}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:btag-calibration", "hepkg:systematic:etmiss-trigger-scale-reso