{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-5901abe9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which generators does analysis 2404.06204 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2404.06204 uses the following generators:\n\n- Comix (matrix-element generator within Sherpa)\n- Herwig 7\n- MadGraph_aMC@NLO FxFx (NLO multijet-merging generator)\n- OpenLoops\n- POWHEG 2.0\n- Photos++ (QED final-state radiation generator)\n- Pythia 8\n- Sherpa\n\nThis list is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For Comix: \"The matrix elements are calculated using the Comix and OpenLoops matrix element generators.\"\n- For Herwig 7: \"Parton showering and hadronization are performed using Herwig 7.\"\n- For MadGraph_aMC@NLO FxFx: \"The NLO multijet-merging is performed using the FxFx prescription in MadGraph_aMC@NLO.\"\n- For OpenLoops: \"The matrix elements are calculated using the Comix and OpenLoops matrix element generators.\"\n- For POWHEG 2.0: \"The POWHEG 2.0 framework is used for the generation of the signal samples.\"\n- For Photos++: \"Final-state QED radiation is simulated using Photos++.\"\n- For Pythia 8: \"Parton showering and hadronization are performed using Pythia 8.\"\n- For Sherpa: \"The matrix elements are calculated using the Comix and OpenLoops matrix element generators within Sherpa.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.04545", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2103.06956", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2110.11231", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2302.05225", "2309.14442", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2404.06204", "2405.18661", "2408.03744", "2504.13081", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "ste