{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-5c841303", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2604.27044 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2604.27044 uses 11 statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n- Barlow-Beeston lite technique for binwise statistical uncertainty modeling\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for SUSY signal strength, background yields and nuisance parameters\n- CMS statistical analysis tool Combine (RooFit/RooStats based)\n- Feldman-Cousins (FC) procedure for coupling modifier interval coverage\n- Fisher F-test for polynomial/basis-function order selection\n- Modified frequentist CLs criterion with asymptotic approximation\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic\n- Quantile matching procedure for validation region input feature alignment\n- Saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test\n- Wilks' theorem asymptotic interpretation of profiled likelihood test statistic\n- k-fold ensembling method for background reweighting DNN variance estimation\n\nThese methods are used to ensure robust and accurate background estimation in the analysis.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2604.27044 uses 11 statistical methods for background estimation, including the Barlow-Beeston lite technique, binned maximum likelihood fit, CMS Combine tool, Feldman-Cousins procedure, Fisher F-test, modified frequentist CLs criterion, profile likelihood ratio, quantile matching, saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test, Wilks' theorem, and k-fold ensembling method.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2009.04363", "2107.12553", "2209.07327", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.27044"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.039}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow-beeston-lite", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-modified-frequentist", "hepkg:method:combine-tool", "hepkg:method:feldman-cousins", "hepkg:method:fisher-f-test", "hepkg:method:k-fold-ensembling", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-ratio", "hepkg:method:quantile-matching", "hepkg:method:saturated-chi2-gof", "hepkg:method:wilks-theorem"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:25b18e888c4e90f56dcef547", "hepkg:evidence:3a15e120794603923eefbcc9", "hepkg:evidence:550e96eec6ef23fefe03d485", "hepkg:evidence:8b4a58c182d86297012e147f", "hepkg:evidence:930f2a5792dc8adb98916c79", "hepkg:evidence:d78598762a1718f66ecc3e35", "hepkg:evidence:dff8fe7d31466c47611ed997"], "seen_values": ["2604.27044", "alignment", "analysis", "and", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "barlow-beeston", "based", "basis-function", "binned", "binwise", "chi-square", "cls", "cms", "combine", "coupling", "coverage", "criterion", "dnn", "ensembling", "estimation", "f-test", "feature", "feldman-cousins", "fisher", "fit", "for", "frequentist", "goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:method:barlow-beeston-lite", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-modified-frequentist", "hepkg:method:combine-tool", "hepkg:method:feldman-cousins", "hepkg:method:fisher-f-test", "hepkg:method:k-fold-ensembling", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-ratio", "hepkg:method:quantile-matching", "hepkg:method:saturated-chi2-gof", "hepkg:method:wilks-theorem", "input", "interpretation", "interval", "k-fold", "likelihood", "lite", "matching", "maximum", "method", "modeling", "modified", "modifier", "nuisance", "order", "parameters", "polynomial", "procedure", "profile", "profiled", "quantile", "ratio", "region", "result_uses_statistical_method", "reweighting", "roofit", "roostats", "saturated", "selection", "signal", "statistic", "statistical", "statistical_method", "strength", "susy", "technique", "test", "th