{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-5f0ca543", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2402.08486 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2402.08486 reports 18 systematic uncertainties. Here they are:\n\n- Color reconnection (CR) model uncertainty (MPI-early-res-on, gluon-move, QCD-inspired)\n- ECAL L1 trigger timing/prefiring inefficiency correction uncertainty (forward endcap, 2016-2017)\n- Flavour-tagging ($b$/$c$/light-jet) efficiency calibration uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy resolution uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) uncertainty (7 independent sources)\n- Lepton identification and isolation efficiency scale factor uncertainty\n- Matrix-element renormalization/factorization scale (mu_r, mu_f) uncertainty\n- PDF (NNPDF3.1, 100 eigenvectors) and alpha_S uncertainty\n- POWHEG hdamp parameter uncertainty\n- Parton shower ISR/FSR scale uncertainty\n- Pileup modeling uncertainty\n- Single top, W+jets, diboson background normalization uncertainty (±30%)\n- Top quark MC mass parameter uncertainty (m_t^MC ± 1 GeV)\n- Trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- Underlying event modeling (CP5 tune parameter) uncertainty\n- W -> l nu branching fraction uncertainty (1.5%)\n- Z+jets background normalization uncertainty (±20%)\n- b hadron semileptonic branching fraction uncertainty\n\nThis list is based on the verbatim sentences from the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2309.14442", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503