{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-5fa503fd", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2207.00348 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2207.00348 uses 11 background-estimation and statistical methods:\n\n- Asimov data set for expected results\n- CL$_{s}$ method for exclusion\n- Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test of background template\n- Gaussian-kernel template smoothing\n- Gaussian/log-normal nuisance-parameter constraint pdfs in likelihood\n- Maximum-likelihood fit to data\n- Principal component analysis of the SMEFT information matrix\n- Profile likelihood technique for CL intervals\n- Pseudo-experiments drawn from background template to validate chi2 p-values\n- Spurious-signal test for background function selection\n- Wald test for background-function selection\n\nThese methods are used to estimate and validate the background in the analysis.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2207.00348 uses 11 background-estimation and statistical methods, including Asimov data set for expected results, CL$_{s}$ method for exclusion, Chi-squared goodness-of-fit test of background template, Gaussian-kernel template smoothing, Gaussian/log-normal nuisance-parameter constraint pdfs in likelihood, Maximum-likelihood fit to data, Principal component analysis of the SMEFT information matrix, Profile likelihood technique for CL intervals, Pseudo-experiments drawn from background template to validate chi2 p-values, Spurious-signal test for background function selection, and Wald test for background-function selection.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2207.00348", "2307.01094"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2207.0