{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-631b1320", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2302.05225 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2302.05225 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Background sample size (bin-by-bin statistical uncertainty of simulated and data-driven backgrounds)\n- Electron and muon experimental uncertainty\n- Flavour tagging uncertainty\n- Hadronic tau decay reconstruction/identification uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet and E_T^miss experimental uncertainty\n- Misidentified background uncertainty (ltau_had)\n- Misidentified background uncertainty (ltau_lprime)\n- Symmetric background estimate statistical uncertainty (Symmetry method)\n- Theoretical uncertainty on Z+jets processes\n- Theoretical uncertainty on diboson processes (6% cross-section)\n- Theoretical uncertainty on signal (Higgs production cross-section)\n- Theoretical uncertainty on top-quark processes\n- Z->ll normalisation uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2510.07527", "2604.21670"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2302.05225"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 14, "error": null, "seconds": 0.046}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:background_sample_size", "hepkg:systematic:electrons_muons", "hepkg:systematic:flavour_tagging", "hepkg:systematic:hadronic_tau_decays", "hepkg:systemat