{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-67fe364a", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many physics processes does analysis 2004.01678 target?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2004.01678 targets 3 physics processes:\n\n- H → Z J/ψ\n- H → Z η_c\n- H → Za (a → hadrons)\n\nThis information is directly extracted from the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.01678"], "predicate": "result_targets_process"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.019}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:process:h-to-z-a", "hepkg:process:h-to-z-etac", "hepkg:process:h-to-z-jpsi"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:001362522490aa3057b9850f", "hepkg:evidence:015d77d6f7a140683784bc0a", "hepkg:evidence:48f508375f2272eb62513958", "hepkg:evidence:f2e6b0c956a52acbe2ea376f"], "seen_values": ["2004.01678", "hadrons", "hepkg:process:h-to-z-a", "hepkg:process:h-to-z-etac", "hepkg:process:h-to-z-jpsi", "physics_process", "result_targets_process"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 8838, "completion_tokens": 178, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 7.028874612879008, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 7.028874612879008, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9016.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 3.0, "evidence_quotes": 4.0}}
{"run_id": "20260814T113003-hepkg-48426", "qid": "gen-paper-680e9b93", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "f506821-dirty", "question": "How many observables does analysis 2112.00895 measure?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2112.00895 measures 9 observables:\n\n1. Differential W+c fiducial cross section as a function of \\( p_T^l \\)\n2. Differential cross section ratio \\( R_c^{\\pm} \\) as a function of \\( p_T^l \\)\n3. Strange quark distribution \\( xs(x, Q^2) \\) and strangeness suppression factor \\( R_s(x, Q^2) \\) from NLO QCD fit\n4. Differential W+c fiducial cross section as a function of \\( | \\eta^l | \\)\n5. Differential cross section ratio \\( R_c^{\\pm} \\) as a function of \\( | \\eta^l | \\)\n6. Charge-specific fiducial cross sections \\( \\sigma(W^+ + \\overline{c}) \\) and \\( \\sigma(W^- + c) \\)\n7. Cross section ratio \\( R_c^{\\pm} = \\frac{\\sigma(W^+ + \\overline{c})}{\\sigma(W^- + c)} \\)\n8. Fiducial W+c production cross section times leptonic branching fraction \\( \\sigma(pp \\to W + c + X) \\times B(W \\to l \\nu) \\)\n9. Goodness of fit of the NLO QCD PDF fit (global chi-squared per degree of freedom)\n\nThese observables cover a range of differential and integrated cross sections, ratios, and fit quality metrics.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2112.00895 measures 9 observables, including differential cross sections, cross section ratios, and fit quality metrics.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2112.00895"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 9, "error": null, "seconds": 0.032}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1b2cdbbcab2bea5670b8ccfb", "hepkg:evidence:1dfd9e4a256f2098575674d1", "